# Independent source-only Flow publication review

The frozen publication plan is accepted for its finite source, licensing and installation mapping contract. This review performs no application, original Node-RED, host, browser, full-suite or benchmark execution and writes nothing into Studio or public evidence.

The final independent collector authenticates the strict83-file plan, all six complete selected payload epochs457/197/64/38/28/38 and eight sidecars,830 exact direct aliases (233 distinct byte identities),19 proposed installation paths (5 current replacements/14 absent additions), two original-cache substitutions, two seed-path substitutions and five documentation overlays. All four test substitutions and all documentation overlays invert to exact frozen source. Every relative documentation link resolves against proposed files, mapped inert aliases or existing files. Runtime files remain exact accepted candidate bytes and do not import an original runtime. The new native-link helper is server-side; this plan proposes no shared-host route change.

Eight selected official Node-RED5.0.8 files and ten verification auxiliary sources remain separately bound. Complete publisher and test-helper Apache-2.0 licenses are preserved in the mapped source epoch. Two exact compressed originals are authenticated but excluded from publication; ignored installed dependencies and generated .local contents are not a complete work-tree census. Nothing claims unique complete source/build correspondence or complete Node-RED runtime/editor parity.

Current18 source before-images, the live737 source fingerprints of the historical937-test receipt, its current753 capsule manifest/source mapping,159 original ID/SHA pairs and232 capability IDs are mandatory. This is source authentication of the prior accepted execution, not a fresh937-test run or a full capsule payload reread. All1681 distinct source rows read in this campaign were stable before/after.

Historical57/75 author campaigns, independent model24 (14 replay/10 fresh), root static7/128 selected compiler calls, old browser8 (7 pass/1 real CRLF failure) and corrected browser12 remain different epochs. Three actual1,812-byte downloads are authenticated exactly. Corrected actual browser proof covers ordinary responses, one chooser import and four Inject runs; held responses, bare-CR browser input and pending disposal remain open. Screenshot bytes were not retained in those browser epochs. No new original/helper/browser invocation is attributed to this review.

Five initial collector attempts failed on reviewer schema assumptions: initial preparation852 rows were incorrectly treated as the final830 alias capture; two explicitly adapted tests were incorrectly required to equal pre-adapter source; heterogeneous registry capability schemas were treated uniformly; a numeric source roster was treated as an array; and historical `passed` fields were treated as corrected `pass` fields. Their exact collector sources, raw outputs and partial source captures/receipts remain in attempts/v1–v5. These were corrected only in this independent collector. Frozen plan/product/original authorities remained unchanged. Additional earlier read-only preparation diagnostics are recorded separately.

Eight fresh in-memory proof mutations reject missing/duplicate aliases, unsafe source paths, incorrect digests, wrong public epochs, archive destinations, an extra cache-helper body change and a missing documentation alias. They are finite metadata guard checks, not product tests. Root owns actual installation and future source-bound focused/full acceptance; no current-layout execution is accepted here.

The source manifests/maps and selected scope/license records in authority/ are exact inert copies. The larger source payloads remain directly authenticated through immutable source-path references rather than recursively copied history. The strict review manifest includes all local review source, raw outputs, unsuccessful attempts, source captures and notices, excluding only its own final self-binding manifest.
